-- R24 - The daily Takeaways reads the weekly MACRO sleeve and prints a MACRO SLEEVE block: it confirms, weakens or
-- flags a signpost on each card and never originates, closes or scores one (both Macro Takeaways digests).
-- Source: thread "Add three-month thematic macro trades", 16 Nov 2026; the owner's "go for all eight".
-- Proposed 16 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule; apply_after = Sun 22 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R24".
-- Text below is byte-identical to the DB row. The sleeve itself: docs/macro_sleeve.md, scripts/macro_sleeve/.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R24' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "MACRO SLEEVE block: the daily run reads the weekly three-month paper book, confirms or weakens each card and flags fired signposts; it never originates, closes or scores a sleeve card", "body": "MACRO SLEEVE (thread \"Add three-month thematic macro trades\", owner's go of 16 Nov 2026). A separate paper book of up to six three-month MACRO cards is written each Sunday evening by the scheduled task \"Macro sleeve weekly\" from the fundamentals pack's regime scorecard (section 1b), the trend monitor, positioning, odds and the credit and cycle lines (docs/macro_sleeve.md in the repo). It is scored apart and is never part of this book's cum R, SCORECARD, TESTED list or thin-edge count. This rule gives the daily run one read and one printed block, and forbids everything else.\n\n1. READ. At the evidence step, in the same pass as the rule reads of spec v19: Google Drive search_files with query exactly `parentId = '1LLeuELL8CLpWmtcywt2DiCpJVopNgyqm' and title contains 'macro_sleeve_current'` (excludeContentSnippets true), take the latest modifiedTime, read_file_content. No file, or a file older than 10 days: print \"MACRO SLEEVE: no current file\" and nothing more.\n\n2. PRINT. A block headed \"MACRO SLEEVE [paper, weekly]\" directly after the TRADE BOOK block, at most 150 words plus one line per card: for each OPEN or PENDING card in the file, \"Mnn <proxy> <long/short> · entry <x> · mark <+/-x.xR> at <today's level from the market pack or the mark script's bars> · <verdict>\" where the verdict is one of CONFIRMED (today's information supports the thesis; say what, <=12 words), UNCHANGED, WEAKENED (<=12 words on why) or SIGNPOST FIRED (name the signpost from the card). The mark is R = direction x (level - entry) / (entry - stop) from the card's META; a pending card prints \"pending\" and no mark. Then one line: \"sleeve scorecard: \" copied from the file's SCORECARD line.\n\n3. NEVER. The daily run never writes a MACRO card, never changes the sleeve file, never closes a sleeve card (a fired signpost is a flag for the Sunday run, which decides), never counts a sleeve card in cum R, the SCORECARD, the TESTED list, the factor count or BOOK CHECK, and never raises or lowers a daily card's p because the sleeve agrees or disagrees. R14 (one direction per underlying) applies inside each book, not across them: a daily card opposite to an open sleeve card is allowed and prints \"against sleeve Mnn\" on its card.\n\n4. DECISION. At 20 closed MACRO cards or on 31 August 2027, whichever is first, the weekly review reads the sleeve file's record and proposes one of: fold the sleeve into this book as a class with its own gate, keep it as a paper book, or stop it. Until then nothing in this book changes because of the sleeve.", "rationale": "The owner asked on 16 Nov 2026 for a second category of roughly three-month macro trades on a cross-country fundamentals base. The existing THEMATIC class is a catalyst class with realised holds of one to two weeks, and the 16 Nov replay of every view the daily run has tested since 5 Oct, held three months with a 3 ATR stop, is a small loss, so a three-month book cannot be the daily views held longer. The sleeve therefore originates weekly from the fundamentals base and the daily run only reports on it. The read is one Drive call and the block is short, so the 08:15 landing is not at risk.", "evidence": "dash.trades (fable) to 16 Nov 2026: 22 closed thematic cards, average 6 days open when stopped, 10 when the target printed, 10 when closed as view changed; 9 of 22 ended at the 10-session review. Replay of 125 view arrivals from dash.tested since 5 Oct as three-month trades (3 ATR stop, 6 ATR target, daily bars): 10 targets, 47 stops, 68 still open, average R near zero and under (counts in the private replay note; nothing matured on the full horizon yet).", "revert_if": "Revert if the Drive read fails on 3 or more runs in a week, if the block costs the 08:15 SGT landing on 2 or more days with no other failure to explain it, or if a daily card is found to have been carded, sized or priced on the sleeve's view (the NEVER list) on 2 or more days.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2027-02-28", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
